WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.050
Bone strength depends on its supporting architecture.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.730
This OpenStax figure provides a view of the trabecular

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:06.060
network.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.670
It is a structural reference, not a patient specimen

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:10.537
from this course.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.165
Chapter forty-four describes osteoporosis
as reduced bone mass with

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.591
an imbalance between resorption and formation.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.830
Watch the supporting connections
thin in this schematic adaptation.

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:27.490
The supplied glucocorticoid pathway
increases RANK ligand and inhibits

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.123
osteoprotegerin, favoring lower bone density.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.993
Less supporting bone means less structural integrity.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.808
Keep that concept separate
from inadequate mineralization of osteoid

00:00:37.838 --> 00:00:38.643
in osteomalacia.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.950
The osteoporosis slides contain
conflicting mineralization wording, so this

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:48.366
film follows the explicit
reduced-mass description on slide thirty-three.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.667
The amount and speed of bone loss shown are

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:51.330
illustrative.
